    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I did:\n\n**Requirement:** Return `checkDigit` = a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`.\n\nSince DTOs are generated from `openapi.yml` at build time via the openapi-generator plugin, and derived fields are populated by MapStruct in `OwnerMapper`, I made three changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit` property (integer, 0\u20139, read-only) to the `Owner` schema, right after `customerCode`. This generates the `checkDigit` field on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/CheckDigitResolver.java`** (new) \u2014 a small resolver, mirroring the existing `MembershipLevelResolver`/`LocalityResolver` pattern, that computes the standard Luhn check digit over the digits of a customer code (ignoring non-digits, null-safe).\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `checkDigit` that calls `CheckDigitResolver.deriveCheckDigit(owner.getCustomerCode())`.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` passes, and the full `./mvnw test` suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
